<%!-- ============================================================
  How it works — the standalone, linkable explainer of the model,
  written for a first-time evaluator: the simplest true version of
  the product, one request traced start to finish.

  The example is the same story the /security hero shows — Maya
  Chen's Claude Code restarting checkout-api.service on api-iad-02,
  approved by Jordan Lee (both from the demo seed) — so the story
  holds across pages. Payload braces are HTML-escaped (&#123;/&#125;)
  because HEEx treats literal braces as interpolation; the colored
  spans follow the home page's code idiom (sky keys, brand strings,
  amber numbers/pending, rose deny).
============================================================ --%>
<div class="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100">
  <.marketing_nav signed_in?={@signed_in?} current={:how_it_works} />

  <%!-- Hero --%>
  <section class="border-b border-zinc-900 bg-[#07080a]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-base font-semibold text-brand-400">How it works</p>
      <.marketing_heading tag="h1" scale={:display} class="mt-2">
        Your agent requests. Your runner executes.
      </.marketing_heading>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
        When your agent needs something done (say a service is failing and it wants to investigate),
        it doesn't open a shell or connect directly to the host. It asks emisar for one declared
        action, on one server, for a stated reason. Depending on your rules, that request runs right
        away, gets refused, or waits for a person to approve it. A small program on your server
        called the runner does the actual work, and every step is written down in the audit log.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- The three parts, then the map that plays how they work together --%>
  <section class="py-20 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white text-balance sm:text-4xl">
          The three pieces.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
          Your AI agent connects to the emisar control plane over MCP. The runner opens an outbound
          TLS WebSocket and exposes no inbound listener. The control plane relays requests and
          results between them and enforces your policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%!-- Wider than the text column, like a product picture: the map needs its three columns. --%>
    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-[75rem] px-6 lg:px-8">
      <.how_it_works_map />
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- Watch it work — the live demo: all three pieces run one real incident end to end. --%>
  <section class="py-24 sm:py-32">
    <div data-reveal class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <p class="text-base font-semibold text-brand-400">Watch it work</p>
        <.marketing_heading tag="h2" scale={:section} class="mt-2">
          Watch a real incident resolve.
        </.marketing_heading>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-400 text-pretty">
          A CSI driver erased 33 hours of metrics by reformatting a live storage volume.
          Follow the agent's investigation, the approved action that stopped further writes,
          and the Terraform fix it prepared for review.
        </p>
      </div>

      <.emisar_demo />
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- How you shape it: one policy for the whole team, then each runner's own rules --%>
  <section class="border-t border-zinc-900 py-20 sm:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white text-balance sm:text-4xl">
          You set the rules once.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
          One person sets the policy for the whole team, so no engineer keeps a private approval
          list for their AI. Every agent in your workspace goes through the same rules.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,3fr)_minmax(0,2fr)]">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/60 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-50">The default policy</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
            Every action has a risk tier, and the tier decides what happens.
          </p>
          <%!-- The four tiers on one track, low to critical, each node lit in its
               decision's color: the mobile menu's gate track (a hairline, nodes cut
               out of it) in the console's policy colors. Each tier is a column of
               five subgrid rows, so a wrapped line can't knock its neighbors out of
               step. Below sm the track runs down the left edge instead. --%>
          <ol class="mt-6 sm:mt-8 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-4">
            <li
              :for={
                {{tier, state, what, example, segment}, index} <-
                  Enum.with_index([
                    {"low", :pass, "Runs right away", "linux.disk_usage",
                     "from-brand-500/50 to-brand-500/50"},
                    {"medium", :pass, "Runs right away", "docker.logs",
                     "from-brand-500/50 to-amber-500/50"},
                    {"high", :pending, "Waits for a person", "nomad.job_revert",
                     "from-amber-500/50 to-rose-500/50"},
                    {"critical", :deny, "Never runs", "kubernetes.drain", nil}
                  ])
              }
              class="relative grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1 py-3 pl-7 sm:row-span-5 sm:grid-cols-1 sm:grid-rows-subgrid sm:justify-items-center sm:gap-0 sm:p-0 sm:text-center"
            >
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 sm:flex-col sm:items-center sm:gap-1">
                <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400">
                  {tier}
                </span>
                <span class="whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-zinc-500">
                  <span class="text-base font-semibold tabular-nums text-zinc-50 sm:text-2xl">
                    {@action_count_by_risk[tier]}
                  </span>
                  actions
                </span>
              </div>
              <span
                class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 w-5 sm:relative sm:mt-5 sm:h-5 sm:w-full sm:justify-self-stretch"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <span
                  :if={segment}
                  class={[
                    "absolute left-1/2 top-6 h-full w-px -translate-x-1/2 bg-linear-to-b sm:hidden",
                    segment
                  ]}
                ></span>
                <span
                  :if={index == 0}
                  class="absolute left-0 top-1/2 hidden h-px w-[400%] -translate-y-1/2 bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,transparent,var(--color-brand-500)_12.5%,var(--color-brand-500)_37.5%,var(--color-amber-500)_62.5%,var(--color-rose-500)_87.5%,transparent)] opacity-50 sm:block"
                ></span>
                <span class={[
                  "absolute left-1/2 top-6 h-2.5 w-2.5 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full ring-[5px] ring-zinc-950 shadow-[0_0_12px_2px] sm:top-1/2",
                  state == :pass && "bg-brand-400 shadow-brand-400/30",
                  state == :pending && "bg-amber-400 shadow-amber-400/30",
                  state == :deny && "bg-rose-400 shadow-rose-400/30"
                ]}></span>
              </span>
              <.state_chip state={state} class="sm:mt-5" />
              <span class="col-span-2 text-sm text-zinc-300 sm:col-span-1 sm:mt-3">{what}</span>
              <span class="col-span-2 font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500 sm:col-span-1 sm:mt-1">
                {example}
              </span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/60 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-50">Your rules come first</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
            Rules match an action pattern, and the first match wins. A runner or a runner group
            can have rules of its own.
          </p>
          <ol class="mt-4 divide-y divide-zinc-900">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-3 py-3">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500">1</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-zinc-200">*.delete_*</code>
              <.state_chip state={:deny} class="ml-auto" />
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-3 py-3">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500">2</span>
              <code class="font-mono text-sm text-zinc-200">nomad.job_*</code>
              <.state_chip state={:pending} class="ml-auto" />
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-3 py-3">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500">3</span>
              <span class="text-sm text-zinc-300">Anything else</span>
              <span class="ml-auto text-sm text-zinc-400">its tier decides</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/60 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-50">A person approves</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
            A request that needs approval waits for one approver or two, in the console or from
            email. Approvals that keep repeating can become standing grants that expire on their
            own.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/60 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-50">Each host has the last word</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
            The runner can allow or deny actions itself and cap the risk it accepts, whatever the
            cloud policy says.
          </p>
          <pre
            phx-no-format
            class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-zinc-900 bg-black/40 p-4 font-mono text-[11.5px] leading-5 text-zinc-300"
          ><span class="text-sky-300">admission</span>:
  <span class="text-sky-300">deny</span>: [<span class="text-brand-300">"*.purge_*"</span>]
  <span class="text-sky-300">max_risk</span>: <span class="text-brand-300">medium</span></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-10 text-center text-sm">
        <.cta_link navigate={~p"/docs/policies-and-approvals"}>Read the policy docs</.cta_link>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- One request, in detail: the map's approval step, field by field --%>
  <section class="border-t border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/40 py-20 sm:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white text-balance sm:text-4xl">
          One request, in detail.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
          Here is the approval step from the map, field by field: an agent asks to end one
          database session that is holding a lock. The names and timings are illustrative.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="mt-14">
        <li class="relative grid grid-cols-[2.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-4 pb-12 sm:gap-x-6">
          <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-5 top-10 w-px bg-zinc-800" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-brand-500/25 bg-brand-500/10 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-brand-400">
            01
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="flex min-h-10 items-center text-base font-semibold text-zinc-50 sm:text-lg">
              The agent asks
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
              The agent picks an action from its catalog and supplies the runner, the arguments,
              and a reason a person can read later.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-900 bg-black/40">
              <div class="border-b border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/80 px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500">
                request summary · not an API payload
              </div>
              <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-4 font-mono text-[11.5px] leading-5 text-zinc-300">&#123;
  <span class="text-sky-300">"tool"</span>: <span class="text-brand-300">"run_action"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"action_id"</span>: <span class="text-brand-300">"postgres.terminate_backend"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"args"</span>: &#123; <span class="text-sky-300">"pid"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">48213</span> &#125;,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"reason"</span>: <span class="text-brand-300">"pid 48213 has held a lock on orders for 9 minutes; checkout writes time out"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"runner"</span>: <span class="text-brand-300">"db-iad-01"</span>
&#125;</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="relative grid grid-cols-[2.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-4 pb-12 sm:gap-x-6">
          <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-5 top-10 w-px bg-zinc-800" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-brand-500/25 bg-brand-500/10 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-brand-400">
            02
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="flex min-h-10 items-center text-base font-semibold text-zinc-50 sm:text-lg">
              emisar checks it
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
              emisar checks that the agent may use this runner, the action belongs to a trusted
              pack, and the arguments are valid. A pack whose hash matches the published catalog
              is trusted automatically. An admin must review and trust custom or modified packs.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-900 bg-black/40">
              <div class="border-b border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/80 px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500">
                the checks
              </div>
              <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-4 font-mono text-[11.5px] leading-5 text-zinc-300"><span class="text-brand-400">✓</span> <span class="text-zinc-500">action</span>   postgres.terminate_backend <span class="text-zinc-500">— in your catalog</span>
<span class="text-brand-400">✓</span> <span class="text-zinc-500">pack</span>     postgres @ 3f9c1e27… <span class="text-zinc-500">— trusted for this account</span>
<span class="text-brand-400">✓</span> <span class="text-zinc-500">args</span>     pid = <span class="text-amber-300">48213</span> <span class="text-zinc-500">— an integer from 1 to 4194304</span>
<span class="text-brand-400">✓</span> <span class="text-zinc-500">runner</span>   db-iad-01 <span class="text-zinc-500">— this agent may use it</span></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="relative grid grid-cols-[2.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-4 pb-12 sm:gap-x-6">
          <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-5 top-10 w-px bg-zinc-800" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-brand-500/25 bg-brand-500/10 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-brand-400">
            03
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="flex min-h-10 items-center text-base font-semibold text-zinc-50 sm:text-lg">
              Your rules decide
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
              Your policy allows the request, refuses it, or holds it for a person. Ending a
              session is high risk, so the default policy holds it, and Jordan approves it before
              the runner starts.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-900 bg-black/40">
              <div class="border-b border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/80 px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500">
                the decision
              </div>
              <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-4 font-mono text-[11.5px] leading-5 text-zinc-300"><span class="text-zinc-500">policy</span>     high risk → the default for its tier
<span class="text-zinc-500">decision</span>   <span class="text-amber-300">require_approval</span> → waiting for a person
<span class="text-zinc-500">approved</span>   <span class="text-brand-300">Jordan Lee · 41 seconds later ✓</span></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="relative grid grid-cols-[2.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-4 pb-12 sm:gap-x-6">
          <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-5 top-10 w-px bg-zinc-800" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-brand-500/25 bg-brand-500/10 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-brand-400">
            04
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="flex min-h-10 items-center text-base font-semibold text-zinc-50 sm:text-lg">
              The runner does the work
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
              The runner checks the request against its installed pack and its local rules, then
              runs the pack's fixed command. It masks secrets that match its patterns before the
              output leaves the host.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-900 bg-black/40">
              <div class="border-b border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/80 px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500">
                on your server
              </div>
              <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-4 font-mono text-[11.5px] leading-5 text-zinc-300"><span class="text-zinc-500">runner</span>   db-iad-01
<span class="text-zinc-500">check</span>    pack hash + arguments — verified again on the host <span class="text-brand-400">✓</span>
<span class="text-zinc-500">run</span>      <span class="text-zinc-500">$</span> <span class="text-zinc-100">psql -XAt -c "SELECT pg_terminate_backend(48213);"</span>
<span class="text-zinc-500">result</span>   exit <span class="text-amber-300">0</span> · 0.04s · t</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="relative grid grid-cols-[2.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-4 sm:gap-x-6">
          <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-brand-500/25 bg-brand-500/10 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-brand-400">
            05
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="flex min-h-10 items-center text-base font-semibold text-zinc-50 sm:text-lg">
              Everything is on the record
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
              Follow the request in the console from approval to result. The audit event links to
              the run, where you can inspect the command and its output.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-900 bg-black/40">
              <div class="border-b border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/80 px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500">
                where to look
              </div>
              <dl class="space-y-4 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-400">
                <div>
                  <dt class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Audit</dt>
                  <dd>The request, the policy decision, Jordan's approval, and the outcome.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Run history</dt>
                  <dd>The arguments, the command, and the redacted output.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Host journal</dt>
                  <dd>
                    A separate record the runner keeps on its own disk, chained line to line.
                  </dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-12 text-center text-sm">
        <.cta_link navigate={~p"/guides/how-emisar-works"}>Read the full technical guide</.cta_link>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <.marketing_cta
    headline="Run your first gated action in five minutes."
    subcopy="Install the runner, connect your agent, and put a real request through."
    secondary_label="Talk to sales"
    secondary_path={EmisarWeb.MailTo.sales()}
  />

  <.marketing_footer />
</div>
